You forget Orcs. The big drawback of Orcs is obviously that their INT is
capped at 16, which means higher failure rates when reading books and
casting spells, and spell casting hunger. But 1/4 of hunger is negligible
and books can be blessed. Spell casting failure rates will improve in
mid-/late-game, when you increase your skills. This leaves a trade-off
between higher failure rates in the early-/mid-game vs. guaranteed poison
resistance from the start, which removes several unavoidable instant
deaths. Give Orcs a chance, Fred.

